# The CRE CLI's own env file. `cre` reads it from the project root — the
# directory holding project.yaml, which is this one — or from an explicit
# `-e/--env` path. Separate from the repo-root .env, which nothing in the CLI
# reads.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in.

# A throwaway EVM account. Nobody issues it — generate one:
#
#     cast wallet new          # Foundry, already a repo dependency
#
# 64 hex characters. A `0x` prefix is accepted and stripped; wrapping quotes are
# not. Use a fresh burner — never a key that holds anything on mainnet.
#
# THREE THINGS NEED IT, and they are worth separating:
#
#   1. `cre account link-key` — signs the transaction that links this address to
#      your CRE account. The linked address is then the workflow owner, and it
#      is the value that goes in the repo-root .env as CRE_WORKFLOW_OWNER, which
#      both receiver contracts pin in the report header. Confirm with
#      `cre account list-key`.
#
#   2. `cre workflow deploy` — registers the workflow in the Workflow Registry.
#      Gated on "Deploy Access" being enabled on your account (`cre whoami`);
#      that is the private beta.
#
#   3. `cre workflow simulate --broadcast` — submits the verdict write through
#      the Arc Testnet MockKeystoneForwarder for real. Fund the address with Arc
#      Testnet gas at https://faucet.circle.com (gas on Arc is USDC, so the same
#      faucet covers gas and any test payment).
#
# A plain (non-broadcast) `cre workflow simulate` needs none of this: the CLI
# falls back to a built-in sentinel key and warns. `--broadcast` rejects that
# sentinel explicitly.
#
# This is a CLI/tooling key, NOT a Verdikt signing identity. The workflow holds
# no key and signs nothing itself — verdicts are DON-signed reports delivered by
# the forwarder (docs/spikes/cre.md, CRE-2).
CRE_ETH_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Shared callback credential. Set this to the same value as the proxy's
# CRE_CALLBACK_TOKEN secret when simulating the verify workflow. This file's
# real .env counterpart is gitignored; never put the value in config JSON.
CRE_CALLBACK_TOKEN_VAR=
